Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hello everyone, welcome back to Munro Live. I'm Kevin, I'm here with Eric and we're here at the Tesla Semi rollout
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.82,0:00:08.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,event for their ride and drive event,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.66,0:00:11.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,the factory tour, and uh hopefully a couple of conversations with the the program team.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.08,0:00:13.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've been here for a little bit. It sounds like we're going
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.02,0:00:16.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,to see get to see quite a bit, which we're pretty excited about.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.26,0:00:19.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um obviously it's a long time coming, so we'll have
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.22,0:00:23.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,to see what they have to offer. So, thanks. We appreciate it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.88,0:00:52.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today everyone, what we're going to do is we'll explain a little bit the process behind stamping, how we go from
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.66,0:00:57.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,this to that.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.06,0:00:58.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,To the final product. Now,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.74,0:01:04.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's uh it's going to be very interesting. We have a video here which we made for you a little bit visually,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.70,0:01:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,so you can you you can refer to my words what I'm saying, okay? So, we have a steel of coil here and what we
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.42,0:01:14.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,essentially do, we throw it onto this CTL, which is a cut-to-length line,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.42,0:01:17.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we cut those blanks each shape and form
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.98,0:01:21.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we need. You see it here. Once this stack of blanks is ready to go,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.14,0:01:24.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,we put it into a tandem line. You can see the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.74,0:01:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,tandem line in the way in the background where you have a couple of streets.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.18,0:01:35.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tandem line is the heart and soul of any stamping operation and it's a beauty.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.86,0:01:41.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a very very sophisticated line, state-of-the-art technology.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.46,0:01:45.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, having said that, how do we make it actually work and run?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.06,0:01:48.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Synchronized, elegant way the way stamping operates.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.64,0:01:54.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,This tandem line consists of five presses,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.38,0:01:55.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,which weigh up to 2,800 tons,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.95,0:02:01.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is roughly 1,400 Model Ys.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.34,0:02:06.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are up to that. So, um but it's and we move hundreds of tons every second.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.02,0:02:10.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we do this? We have up to 600 sensors installed in this line.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.16,0:02:13.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,They all talk to each other. Every stroke signals
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.74,0:02:20.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,talk to each other in milliseconds. And all the 600 sensors, they have to say yes before anything moves.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.58,0:02:27.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we have also job data. Every part that you see, final part, has to 7,000 to 8,000 job data behind it. You
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.86,0:02:30.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,change one there, you change the part.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.26,0:02:35.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, two things that we do very different than any Tesla plant in the world. One is the handshake.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.78,0:02:37.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I call it the kiss.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.38,0:02:40.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Go open the oil again. It's the automation how we hand over the parts when
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.96,0:02:45.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,we have an idle station. And the other one is the in-die clinching. We
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.86,0:02:53.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,attach the fasteners in our stamping process inside the We don't need a lot of floor space. It's one machine, one
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.34,0:02:56.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,footprint. No more stud cells,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.30,0:03:00.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,no more nut cells. Now,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.78,0:03:01.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Keith, tell me what about those dies?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.40,0:03:05.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good afternoon. My name's Keith Dworak.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.46,0:03:08.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm the staff tooling guy engineer for sub assembly here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.50,0:03:15.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Once we get the blanks while they're in his group, they come into our between three or five processes they go
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.46,0:03:18.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,into the press. Each process does something different.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.19,0:03:23.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It takes in On the first one is form, then it will trim,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.30,0:03:29.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,pierce, re-strike, and then put out. We have two open up here. This one here is a trim die over to my right. Three.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.46,0:03:36.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And over here is four. This is a the re-strike here and flange. Once it goes through there,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.50,0:03:43.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,it comes to the end of line where our quality department will take and put it on the static fixture here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.26,0:03:44.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's a series of pins and gauges that go on here to
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.68,0:03:49.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,ensure that every part is trimmed the same, pierced the same,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.58,0:03:56.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,they're all the same. Once that goes together, it's a beautiful thing. We make trucks. However, we're not done yet
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.82,0:03:59.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,because we want to make sure that y'all get you the
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.55,0:04:04.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,best part quality that you can. So, we send each one
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.74,0:04:07.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,into a scanner system that you see here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.42,0:04:10.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It has the data in a computerized automated design.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.86,0:04:15.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,You take that data with what we get from here and it shows there. If it's green,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.14,0:04:18.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's beautiful. That's what we shoot for.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.58,0:04:20.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what we get all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.18,0:04:23.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I would be remiss if I didn't say that everything that you're
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.55,0:04:27.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,about to see as you go through here has come through our
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.90,0:04:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,line. We do 62 part numbers going through here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.18,0:04:33.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's hundreds of parts that you can see as you're surrounded here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.30,0:04:35.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of them, the highest world-class quality we can
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.79,0:04:40.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,possibly produce at the quickest, most efficient way possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.06,0:04:44.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Obviously, Tesla's doing a lot of in-house stamping. From what we saw uh there and what was presented, it looks
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.86,0:04:52.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,like they essentially have a single kind of tandem line there for uh for stamping, blanking, and all the the
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.14,0:04:53.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,subsequent operations and trimming.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.94,0:04:59.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,I didn't see any other stations like that. So, um when we kind of walked up into the station where they briefed, we
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.46,0:05:03.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,are flanked on every side on each side, I should say,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.70,0:05:09.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,um by a ton of essentially like very densely packed stampings. So, it suggests to me, based on what we could
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.38,0:05:10.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,see here, that they've got not a ton of presses running um
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.96,0:05:14.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,and given the volume of 50,000 units, it kind of makes sense
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.50,0:05:22.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,that they're going to run bankable parts, swap out tools, batch build another set of parts, and then continue
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.18,0:05:23.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,that process um meeting essentially like I said, bank building,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.43,0:05:27.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,building all that inventory up, and then keeping their
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.38,0:05:32.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,essentially presses running um and highly utilized uh essentially through the entire process. So, just one thing I
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.34,0:05:34.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,wanted to kind of point out um when we're going through the stamping uh aspect
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.91,0:05:38.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,of it cuz literally as we were walking into the building, it took a
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.42,0:05:44.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,little bit to get to there. It's off to the left-hand side and just the entire left-hand side is essentially just
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.14,0:05:45.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,stacked uh stamped parts, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.50,0:05:48.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,ready for assembly. And then the far right side was essentially assembly cells and
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.76,0:05:52.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,the powder coating cells as well. And a key point there, we'll talk
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.54,0:05:55.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,a little bit more about it, but we walked right in.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.66,0:05:57.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,They obviously weren't running anything,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.74,0:06:01.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,but there's no hazmat areas or anything like that. We walked right into the line. The powder coating cells were off
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.58,0:06:07.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,the right-hand side. Just a big advantage of the uh powder coating over your kind of traditional liquid paint cells
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.86,0:06:12.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,um with respect to kind of what you need to do to maintain um a paint shop like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.86,0:06:19.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm the manufacturing engineer for uh top cover and the visual battery factors. Uh the part that I simply use
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.18,0:06:26.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,here on my left as enclosure and then the one you see on the right as top cover. They assemble together to form
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.70,0:06:28.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh high voltage structural housing or uh battery assembly.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.82,0:06:33.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, as you can see this assembly, we spend a good time
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.94,0:06:39.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,to develop uh an optimal number of components so that we
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.26,0:06:41.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,can achieve the best uh kilowatt per hour per uh per
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.50,0:06:46.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,weight of each each assemblies. Uh just to put it into
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.74,0:06:49.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,perspective, uh as you can see this is the size of
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.46,0:06:55.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,our residential bathtub and then the weight is similar to a
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.46,0:06:57.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,commercial refrigerator. Um so, we like this is the uh enclosure
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.64,0:07:01.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,and the top cover lines as well. We We have more
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.98,0:07:08.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,than 100 robots and then we use advanced automation uh technology and then different fixture and strategies as well
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.42,0:07:15.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then different uh assembly technologies uh which my friend Selo will explain later about the processes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.54,0:07:22.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um to keep the part to the highest quality standard, we are going we are using 100% inline inspection and then
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.98,0:07:28.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,vision-assisted dimensional uh tolerance uh offset as well. Um so,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.58,0:07:34.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,once the line is complete in in our line, it will go to a downstream application which is e-coat process.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.74,0:07:38.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,After the e-coat, it goes to high voltage battery assembly line
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.70,0:07:43.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,which you will see later in your tour. I'll give
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.18,0:07:45.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,my I'll give it to my friend Cello.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.70,0:07:51.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Evenet. Welcome everybody. My name is Cello. I've been with Tesla since 3 years. I'm responsible for
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.26,0:07:52.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,joining and process engineering.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.30,0:07:54.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,So,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.06,0:07:57.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,to put them together, we use three different joining technologies for the battery
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.16,0:08:01.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,top cover and for the battery enclosure, we use six different joining
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.30,0:08:07.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,technologies. In total, we have seven different joining technologies. For example, at the battery top cover, you
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.42,0:08:10.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,can see here the gold line, it's a laser brazing seam.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.28,0:08:15.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We use laser brazing, we have resistance spot welds, we have
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.58,0:08:22.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,structural adhesives. On the battery enclosure side, we have mark welds, we have resistance spot welds as well,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.10,0:08:24.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,structural adhesives, drawn arc welds.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.42,0:08:30.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,We do have projection welding. We do also multi-material mix between steel and aluminum. That's the reason we also
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.62,0:08:37.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,use self-piercing rivets. Um just to get an idea how many spot welds we have here, for long range truck, we have we
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.26,0:08:42.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,need three battery structures. That means per battery structure, we have 1,000 spot welds.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.54,0:08:46.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with three battery structures, we would be at 3,000 spot welds.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.04,0:08:49.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Compared to the cab from the Semi, we would have
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.70,0:08:51.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,the we would have the 2,800 spot welds.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.70,0:08:56.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we do have more spot welds at the battery systems than at the entire cab.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.46,0:09:05.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the next thing we saw was essentially the battery tray itself. Um kind of off the side, it's it's it's
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.06,0:09:08.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,primarily steel. As you can kind of see here off to the right, a series of stampings.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.82,0:09:11.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um each one of their modules essentially slot in horizontally.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.98,0:09:15.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,We did get to see um a battery that was deleted. We could
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.98,0:09:19.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,see inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.06,0:09:19.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we were asked not to film that. Um I don't want to speak
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.62,0:09:23.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,too much about it and kind of respect that, but at a high
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.14,0:09:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,level, it reminded me a lot of essentially an early Model S pack. Um the big thing that I took away from that
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.18,0:09:32.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,is, like everything with the Semi truck,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.66,0:09:34.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,serviceability. So, as you know, as we have seen the
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.01,0:09:40.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,progression essentially from uh the use of aluminum extrusions,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.86,0:09:42.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,castings into and their battery packs,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.14,0:09:48.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,then the transition essentially with your later Model Y's, Model 3's and such to the stamp packs. We essentially
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.14,0:09:51.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tesla's one of the few companies we've seen numerous generations of packs being uh,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.89,0:09:55.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,iterated and put into the marketplace. Um, so seeing a primarily
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.74,0:09:59.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,steel pack here is exactly what I expected to see. Um, I was a little um,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.98,0:10:02.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,surprised to see and I don't want to say lack of integration,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.20,0:10:05.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,but when I when we saw inside that essentially um, it's
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.50,0:10:12.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,clear that they um, balanced that decision out favoring serviceability and long service life
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.30,0:10:13.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,with the pack and the modules itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.74,0:10:17.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it looked like everything that we saw that was loaded into here,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.48,0:10:21.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,the cassettes of uh, 4680s um, was serviceable.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.06,0:10:22.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,But as you can kind of look through here and I
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.13,0:10:25.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,was having a brief conversation with Jordan, he didn't necessarily know
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.82,0:10:30.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,where the orientation and frankly even when I first walked in, I kind of thought this was longitudinally oriented
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.06,0:10:32.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,and this was looking at from the side of the vehicle uh,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.30,0:10:36.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,just based off of the structure that is present on the side of
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.06,0:10:40.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,the pack. So, they have like a dedicated section on the upper part which is supporting the mounting to the pack to
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.86,0:10:44.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,the frame and then they have essentially some outriggers on the lower portion.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.62,0:10:48.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, but that's actually it's transversely mounted.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.78,0:10:54.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is actually these cutouts here are for the main frame rail sections and essentially they have cross members
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.50,0:10:59.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,running across the top um, and the side and they kind of fills the entire cavity of um,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.78,0:11:04.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,on a traditional truck where you would essentially see fuel tanks,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.62,0:11:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,um, exhaust aftertreatment, storage boxes and things of that nature. On the Tesla Semi, it's the batteries
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.42,0:11:17.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,essentially running um, cross car all the way out to probably if I had to guess maybe a
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.66,0:11:19.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,a 400 3 to say 500 mm threshold of your outer aero skirts.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.82,0:11:23.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then you essentially get to um, a series of uh,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.88,0:11:29.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,structures that they build off this. Um, but really when you look
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.06,0:11:32.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,at it, I mean it looks a lot like essentially a a frame on a truck.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.16,0:11:36.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I fully expected that this was actually, you know, or
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.42,0:11:38.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,oriented to the front and and and interfacing with the cradle
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.16,0:11:41.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,and whatever they were doing for the rear drive modules.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.42,0:11:47.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I felt a little silly when I finally saw them oriented in vehicle and and saw that. Um
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.78,0:11:50.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, you know, again, lots of use of castings, excuse me,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.10,0:11:56.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,um of stampings throughout this. Small use of essentially redundant uh castings here
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.10,0:11:59.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,for all the um outer nodes. There's a unique one for the inner provisions.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.22,0:12:06.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,They all look like they can slip a little bit in Z. Um these lower um weldments here, I was a
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.58,0:12:10.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,little prior to little surprised to see that they were essentially a big weldment. A lot of MIG welding going on
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.66,0:12:13.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,here. We don't see MIG welding, I think,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.06,0:12:18.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,anywhere else in the plant um besides here. So, makes me kind of wonder where this is being done based off of
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.66,0:12:22.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,everything else we saw there. It wouldn't surprise me to see these turn into a casting in the future, but there
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.58,0:12:24.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,might be a very deliberate reason why they are doing this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.59,0:12:27.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I just couldn't tell from just looking at it. But, you
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.82,0:12:31.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,can kind of see there's an internal bulkhead here.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.66,0:12:34.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, um where this external mounting interface here is, what uh is here,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.32,0:12:38.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,what complements this is essentially a large cast U-shape
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.42,0:12:40.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,bulkhead. You can see a little bit of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.46,0:12:42.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,We didn't have a better picture of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.22,0:12:48.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll try and get one uh or ask some friends if we can get a better shot um from inside the pack itself. And then
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.98,0:12:54.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,that is complemented by two stampings that provide that section that runs across. And this complements this area
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.94,0:13:00.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,here on the top where the frames are running through. So, realistically, all those loads, if there was an impact,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.06,0:13:02.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,whether it's from the front, the rear,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.06,0:13:04.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,or anything like that, um these these packs are daisy chained together.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.65,0:13:07.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,This would run up if this was a four-pack up
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.50,0:13:10.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,into the chassis and then your subsequent mid and uh rear packs are also
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.35,0:13:14.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,kind of daisy chained off this in a big structural bulkhead. This made me
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.90,0:13:22.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,really think of essentially modern aircraft. Have you ever seen how like an F-18 and F-35 are actually really like
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.50,0:13:26.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,an F-14 big huge titanium bulkhead um you know, within it. And actually a pretty interesting process. That's why
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.26,0:13:30.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,they scrapped them all um after they were decommissioned. But, overall,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.90,0:13:38.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,exactly kind of what we expected to see is um a series of stampings and a low-cost, you know, kind of strategy for
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.86,0:13:40.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,their battery pack itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.58,0:13:43.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome to main line. Uh it's really exciting to share with you
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.64,0:13:47.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,all the final assembly of the Semi cabin, which is the
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.74,0:13:49.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,the trail of the Semi.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.78,0:13:54.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I'm Carlos as the process engineer for this body line.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.54,0:13:59.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm Shreya Gorey. I'm the process engineering technician for body in white.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.94,0:14:06.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, here at the frame station, we put our main cabin together. We have our
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.22,0:14:09.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,body side left, body side right, and underbody that come together.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.45,0:14:13.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're closed together, and then we have our
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.50,0:14:19.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,roof that comes on as the cherry on the top. So, we weld our
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.50,0:14:23.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,cabin together. We also have two important joining technologies here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.78,0:14:27.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have resistance spot welding and
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.42,0:14:31.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,structural adhesive that is used to put this cabin together.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.94,0:14:39.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Once we put the cabin together, we send it to our robotic vision inspection system. From there, it goes to our
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.10,0:14:45.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,end-of-line station, where we do our final uh quality checks before it goes to final assembly.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.74,0:14:48.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next thing we saw was essentially the body in white.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.86,0:14:54.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, they didn't talk too much about this, but as you can kind of see, it's primarily all aluminum. I don't know if
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.10,0:14:56.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's numerous grades. What we kind of saw on the inner A-pillar here,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.50,0:14:59.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,more specifically in that picture there, you
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.22,0:15:05.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,can kind of see um it's a slightly different hue. It might be a different grade, but uh there was nothing about
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.70,0:15:08.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh the processing of coils as they kind of came in, where they talked about anything about surface treatments or
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.94,0:15:12.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,different grades being used in the plant. Um so, it could just be excuse me,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.75,0:15:16.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,the light being thrown a particular way off of how
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.18,0:15:19.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,this was illuminated, or it could be a different grade. Um but, primarily,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.17,0:15:21.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,um all large stampings, and and can kind of
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.70,0:15:28.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,see through these These these aren't really being kicked together. Big stamping, big aperture piercing here
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.02,0:15:30.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,and relatively limited use of castings.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.10,0:15:31.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.74,0:15:34.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,on the front upper A-pillar and the front header here,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.05,0:15:39.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's a unit casting here or a nodal casting and same thing on the other side.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.90,0:15:44.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then in the front of the vehicle here on this kind of horse collar structure,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.10,0:15:48.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,so the floor is here as it comes across. This is kind of a
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.54,0:15:53.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,an underfloor cab rail. The face of that running across the lower portion of the dash pad,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.38,0:16:00.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,that's all cast, it's a single piece and we have steel crush cans themselves there. I don't think I saw any other
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.22,0:16:04.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,steel parts that were e-coated. They typically do this for corrosion.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.78,0:16:06.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,There could be some essentially in seat mounts or restraint mounts like
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.69,0:16:11.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,tap it plates elsewhere within the vehicle and they would essentially be
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.26,0:16:14.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,e-coated like that as well and then captivated somewhere else within the vehicle.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.81,0:16:18.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I didn't see any other steel there. Again, in general we were
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.66,0:16:22.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,we were moved along pretty quickly through each one of these stations just given the number of people that were
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.54,0:16:23.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,coming through after us.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.62,0:16:26.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but high-level,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.74,0:16:29.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, there's when I look at this a little bit smoother
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.21,0:16:33.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,load paths than most trucks. You have a very forward seating
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.30,0:16:40.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,position. The cab wraps around you quite a bit. So, essentially the seating the seat is here,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.54,0:16:46.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,but unlike most vehicles, this kind of balances a little bit of essentially cab over features and your kind of
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.50,0:16:53.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,traditional, you know, engine out front cab behind orientation, but you get essentially body structure that wraps
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.10,0:16:54.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,around you with the hinge pillar on more conventional trucks would be
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.51,0:16:57.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,much closer to where you would expect to see it as
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.38,0:17:03.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,you open the door, get right into the seat. Where here essentially you have essentially the door ring the and the
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.18,0:17:05.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,hinge pillar being one here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.94,0:17:07.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And essentially that's all fixed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.42,0:17:12.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nothing there moves. Your window regulator, all that stuff goes to a very fixed point on the body.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.06,0:17:15.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, very different than what we typically see and frankly I think you
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.60,0:17:19.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,can really tell that you know, this is a a Semi truck that's
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.86,0:17:22.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,being built by an auto manufacturer.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.06,0:17:27.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just again, the smooth load paths, the crush cans, I've never really seen so much deliberate energy management in a
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.62,0:17:33.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,lot of these kind of class eight vehicles that we kind of I looked around very very briefly, just looking through
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.54,0:17:34.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, your Freightliners, your Macs,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.54,0:17:36.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,your Volvos, and some of those other vehicles.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.47,0:17:40.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,They essentially disassociate all structure um from the cab forward of
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.94,0:17:47.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,the vehicle cuz realistically, it's it's engine, it's almost like a I don't know the best way to put it,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.22,0:17:53.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,like an immovable object when you really get down to it of how much um space is is taken there, and frankly, what
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.18,0:17:59.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,energy, if you were in an impact, is being absorbed there or hits, and how it reacts to the rest of the vehicle.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.62,0:18:00.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I think uh this is Suchi Kesh.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.04,0:18:03.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm the process engineer for the body weight shop.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.56,0:18:05.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh this is body weight area for
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.02,0:18:11.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,high roof assembly. Uh so, let me give you some background about high roof and its manufacturing line. So, this
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.86,0:18:18.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,aerodynamic assembly is manufactured entirely from aluminum material to reduce the overall vehicle weight while
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.26,0:18:24.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,maintaining its structural strength. Uh it also uh Uh we have the uh joining technologies,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.70,0:18:31.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,different joining technologies, such as uh resistance spot welding, clinching process, and also our adhesive
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.26,0:18:35.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,application process uh to create this uh whole joint assembly.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.14,0:18:38.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh the stage the production of the high roof is divided into two stages.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.05,0:18:41.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,First one is the high roof bracket line, where
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.34,0:18:43.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,we join all the small brackets on together by using the joining
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.83,0:18:48.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,technologies and transfer it to the downstream process. And the second stage
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.66,0:18:53.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,is the high roof uh assembly line, where we uh join the side skin, uh top skin,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.42,0:18:58.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,and uh by using those brackets and create the finished whole assembly. At the end of the process, we unload this
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.98,0:19:04.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,finished whole assembly on the conveyor and send it to the pre-coat, which is the downstream process for the whole
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.66,0:19:05.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,body weight shop.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.08,0:19:12.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hello everyone. My name is David Couples. I'm the associate manager for body and white and coatings. Uh as Suchi
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.74,0:19:14.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Kesh said, there's a lot of complex engineering and manufacturing
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.01,0:19:17.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,that goes into the production of one of these high
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.02,0:19:19.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,roofs. We'll walk a little bit more into the benefits the
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.75,0:19:24.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Semi gets from having them high roof manufactured this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.06,0:19:29.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,The number that may surprise you is that this high roof only weighs about 170 lb,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.78,0:19:34.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it has over 700 welds on it. That's a lot of manufacturing that goes into a product that's this light. Not only
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.46,0:19:36.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,that,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.34,0:19:38.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,we just don't build the high roof to add another structure to the cabin.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.41,0:19:42.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We don't just build a high roof to make it have that sleek design that makes it look
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.02,0:19:49.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,really cool going down the road. We build the high roof to improve our aerodynamics. So, that said, as the
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.66,0:19:55.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,cabin moves down the highway, and there's a lot of air that pushes up against it, the high roof helps redirect
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.82,0:20:03.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,that air over the trailer. It gives us more range. It gives us a better energy efficiency. That said, that's super
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.34,0:20:08.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,important for a class 8 vehicle. This going to spend most of its life riding up and down the freeway at highway
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.46,0:20:15.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,speeds. That's a lot of air to move around. And ultimately, we're trying to hit that 1.7 kW per hour
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.14,0:20:18.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,per mile to give us that effective range for our long-range vehicles
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.18,0:20:22.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,of 500 miles for a full charge. That said, every time
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.14,0:20:24.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,we produce one of these, we're not just producing another part.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.47,0:20:28.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we're doing is we're producing a functional part of
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.18,0:20:35.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,a system that really takes mechanical precision and translates that over to aerodynamic efficiency, energy
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.06,0:20:38.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,efficiency, and ultimately vehicle range.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.34,0:20:42.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Guys, my name is Jay. This is Marco, and this is the coatings line.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.82,0:20:48.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tesla's legacy vehicle manufacturing facilities are built around a technology that has
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.82,0:20:51.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,been the industry standard for decades, liquid paint.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.04,0:20:58.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,When we designed this uh, sub uh,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.26,0:21:05.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Semi we didn't just design a new truck, we designed a manufacturing
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.70,0:21:07.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,process from the ground up.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.74,0:21:14.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,We challenged every coating requirement we have. Corrosion protection, UV stability,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.74,0:21:20.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,long-term durability, stone chip resistance, and of course, aesthetics.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.38,0:21:23.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,We asked ourselves, does it have to be liquid paint?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.94,0:21:25.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the answer was no.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.74,0:21:31.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we turned to powder coating, which we actually have a lot of experience with from our energy products.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.10,0:21:35.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,But to make powder coating work at this scale,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.82,0:21:39.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,we had to make some deliberate engineering decisions from day one,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.98,0:21:45.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,which meant selecting the right substrate, the correct fastening material and methods.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.80,0:21:53.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we also influenced part geometry.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.22,0:21:57.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the results are this coatings line you see behind me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.82,0:22:02.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,This line is 1/3 the size of a equivalent liquid paint line.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.42,0:22:07.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,It has less waste, essentially zero VOCs,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.74,0:22:13.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we think it brings the best value to our customers.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.42,0:22:15.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Marco will walk you through the process.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.46,0:22:18.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you everyone, and thank you for being here.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.54,0:22:26.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh coating system makes a step on the process, where we give the preparation of surface. We have two main processes
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.70,0:22:30.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,to do that. The first one already Rob mentioned, we have a pre-treatment,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.34,0:22:37.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,where we clean all the surfaces and prepare with the first layer, so we can prepare all the surface to add and get
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.14,0:22:39.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,bond the paint.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.50,0:22:43.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,After that, we seal it the cabin, so it is prepared for the road.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.06,0:22:48.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the last part and the main is where we do the magic come from.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.10,0:22:50.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,We spray the powder color to give every part of
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.41,0:22:54.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,the body the color that we are uh uh
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.78,0:22:57.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,well, delivering to our clients. So,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.22,0:23:03.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,these many layers of protection give us all the warranty that we are giving a last longer duration,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.58,0:23:09.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,and give us a high durability on our buses. Thank you so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.10,0:23:13.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the next station, I believe um actually there's roofs prior to this,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.54,0:23:15.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,but we can kind of speak to that here as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.70,0:23:17.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um So, I'll kind of go into that very, very briefly. So,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.91,0:23:22.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,when you look at the truck and it's kind of overall aero feature on
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.14,0:23:26.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,top, um and cuz it kind of ties in with essentially the other panels that are here. So, generally speaking on the a
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.50,0:23:27.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,lot of these vehicles,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.26,0:23:30.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,um your hoods, your fenders, your aero skirts,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.52,0:23:36.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,um and everything realistically kind of your big class A surfaces are
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.54,0:23:39.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,typically composite. Um there's nothing necessarily wrong with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.98,0:23:46.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,They often time are essentially like a slurry of a fiberglass or a rolled mat, something to that that effect.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.10,0:23:50.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,They often times are relatively heavy, they're large, and um they're expensive.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.94,0:23:57.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have some I personally have some very direct experience with dealing with large composite panels, and sometimes
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.02,0:24:04.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,they're they're absolute right call, um but I can see exactly why a lot of the
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.06,0:24:09.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,features and panels that we'd see on more traditional trucks, Tesla brought in-house, stamped them, and then powder
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.62,0:24:11.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,coated them. So,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.54,0:24:15.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,um nothing too, too crazy as far as the the roof aero there, since they have large panels,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.14,0:24:19.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,a little bit of buckling that we kind of saw, but realistically,
